>> result completely self-contained entities. {lo nu mi do cinba} forms one
>> single object that doesn't depend on the containing bridi.
>>
>> As for {su'u}, it turns out that it's simply a vague abstractor, and
>> that's it. It's a stand-in for any regular abstractor, and its type is
>> completely context-dependent. Although this has never really happened as
>> far as I know, it would, however, be possible to create new types of
>> abstractors by means of su'u2.
